        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>In a blast furnace, iron is extracted from haematite ($Fe_2O_3$) through a reduction process where carbon monoxide (CO) acts as the reducing agent. The CO is produced from the reaction of coke (carbon) with oxygen. The other options (hydrogen, nitrogen, and chlorine) are not used in this process.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
